  "body": "**What.** Decide and write down the criterion for reproducing a computer-assisted bound on another machine or build, then apply it to #104. Recommended by win2 in #104's summary.\n\n**Why.** #104's criterion, overlapping \u03c1\u2086\u2090 balls, treated \u03c1\u2086\u2090 as the enclosure of one number. It is an upper bound computed from an enclosure B, and an adaptive validated integration can build different valid B on different platforms. The two choices are:\n- make the non-rigorous steps, such as step-size control, platform-deterministic, so that bounds can be required to agree;\n- accept a reproduction when each run's own bound is valid and passes (\u03c1\u2086\u2090 < 1), each reported, and require the stored-enclosure cross-loads (#110) to reproduce each other's bounds exactly.\n\n**Acceptance (can fail).** The criterion is written into AGENTS.md (\"Computer-assisted proofs\") and proof/A_lemmas_M.md, and #104 then passes or fails under it.\n\n**Depends on.** #110.\n",
