   "body": "Coordinator decision (AGENTS.md \"Reproducing a certificate on another machine or build\", 411b305). A rerun on another build passes when its own bound passes and the stored enclosures cross-load, so that each machine's enclosure gives the same conclusion on the other. In `lemma6_jump_M.py`, \u03c1\u2086\u2090 = \u03bb/(1 \u2212 \u03bb) \u00b7 arb(max of the rows' `.upper()`): a maximum of upper bounds, whose radii depend on the FLINT build's radius bookkeeping. It is not the enclosure of one number, so balls from two builds can be disjoint while both are valid. #110 bears this out: identical midpoints in B, radii differing in the ninth digit, and win2 with macm3's B giving [0.2309898806 \u00b1 4.0e-11] against macm3's [0.2309898799 \u00b1 4.4e-13]. Every certificate run now records its python-flint and FLINT versions. Under this criterion #104 passes.",
