   "body": "Coordinator correction (db61773): my reason above, \"radii depend on the FLINT build\", was wrong. Both machines run FLINT 3.6.0 (#110, macm3's half). Most of the gap is the reload: arb rounds each stored radius up to its 30-bit mag, inflating every radius by 1e-9 to 5e-9 relative and moving \u03c1\u2086\u2090 by about 6e-10 (macm3's own B reloaded gives [0.2309898805 \u00b1 3.1e-11]). The rest is the integrations' radii differing in the ninth digit. The criterion stands unchanged.",
